# Scarborough Fair - traditionele Engelse ballade
# Traditionele Noord-Engelse ballade, verwant aan "The Elfin Knight" (Child 2, tot
# 1670 terug te voeren); de bekende melodie werd in 1947 door Ewan MacColl opgetekend.
# Simon & Garfunkel maakten het in 1966 bekend in een bewerking naar Martin Carthy
# (Wikipedia (en), "Scarborough Fair (ballad)"). Tekst en wijs publiek domein; de
# akkoorden volgen de gangbare bewerking.
# Overgenomen uit SCARBORO.GHF (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Tikfout hersteld: "Tell here" werd
# "Tell her". Het bestand bevat daarna nog een kort Nederlands lied; dat staat
# apart als samen-trekken-wij-naar-de-hei.
{title: Scarborough Fair}
{meta: id scarborough-fair}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit SCARBORO.GHF (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via Wikipedia (en), Scarborough Fair (ballad)}
{meta: tag volkslied}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{key: Em}

{start_of_verse}
[Em]Are you going to [D]Scarborough [Em]Fair
[G]Parsley, [Em]sage, rosema[G]ry [A]and [Em]thyme
Remember me to [G]someone who [F#]lives [Em][D]there
She [Em]once was a [D][Em]true [D]love [Em]of [D][Em]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Tell her to make me a cambric shirt
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
Without no seams nor needle work
Then she'll be a true love of mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Tell her to find me an acre of land
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
Between the salt water and the sea strands
Then she'll be a true love of mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Tell her to reap it with a sickle of leather
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
And gather it all in a bunch of heather
Then she'll be a true love of mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Are you going to Scarborough Fair
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
Remember me to one who lives there
She once was a true love of mine
{end_of_verse}
